go 1.25.0

// The workspace composes the SDK and the product modules from source during
// local development, so a change to the SDK is testable before it is tagged.
//
// It declares no replacements. sdk/v0.2.0 is published, so every module
// requires a version the module proxy can serve and nothing here has to stand
// in for it.
//
// One replacement is permitted, and only while an SDK release is in flight: the
// release gate compares its tag against the version modules/reference requires,
// so that requirement names the new version before the tag exists, and the Go
// tool cannot build a module graph that requires a version with no revision.
// TestTheWorkspaceReplacesNothingOutsideAnSDKReleaseWindow permits exactly that
// one and nothing else, and the procedure is in
// docs/reference/release-artifacts.md under "Releasing a version nothing is
// built against yet".
//
// Committed replace directives remain prohibited in every go.mod; the workspace
// is the sanctioned place for one. See docs/plans/first-cli-vertical-slice.md
// section 4 and docs/adr/0009-sdk-versioning-and-publication.md.
use (
	.
	./modules/reference
	./sdk
)
